---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';
const title='Privacy Policy | VoxelCurve';
const description='How VoxelCurve handles local build progress, blueprint links, browser-generated exports and hosting data.';
const canonical='https://voxelcurve.com/privacy';
const schemas=[breadcrumbSchema([{name:'VoxelCurve',url:'https://voxelcurve.com/'},{name:'Privacy Policy',url:canonical}])];
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} {canonical} {schemas}>
  <section class="resource-hero"><div class="container"><div class="resource-hero-grid">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span><h1>Local-first by default.</h1><p>VoxelCurve is designed to work without an account and keeps build completion progress in your browser.</p></div>
    <div class="resource-meta"><span>LAST UPDATED</span><strong>October 4, 2026</strong><small>This policy describes the current production site.</small></div>
  </div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container editorial-grid">
    <aside class="editorial-aside"><div class="section-kicker">01 / Data flow</div><p>What stays on your device and what may reach infrastructure providers.</p></aside>
    <div class="prose editorial-prose">
      <h2>No account required</h2>
      <p>VoxelCurve does not currently require user registration or a VoxelCurve account to generate or use blueprints.</p>
      <h2>Geometry and exports</h2>
      <p>Blueprint calculations run in your browser. PNG images, SVG blueprints, printable plans, TXT plans, QR codes and supported Litematic files are generated client-side. VoxelCurve does not intentionally upload those generated files to an application server.</p>
      <h2>Local build progress</h2>
      <p>Completion progress may be stored in browser local storage so a build can be resumed on the same browser and device. Clearing site data, using private browsing, switching browsers or changing devices may remove or make that progress unavailable.</p>
      <h2>Shared blueprint links</h2>
      <p>Shape settings can be encoded in the URL fragment after the <code>#</code>. The shared state can include dimensions, style and thickness. Completion progress and material labels are not included in the shared blueprint fragment.</p>
      <p>URL fragments are normally handled by the browser and are not sent to the web server as part of the HTTP request. A person or service you deliberately share the full link with can still see the fragment.</p>
      <h2>Hosting and network data</h2>
      <p>VoxelCurve is delivered through Cloudflare Pages and related Cloudflare infrastructure. Like other websites, infrastructure providers may process standard request and security information such as IP address, user agent, requested URL, timestamps and network/security signals as needed to deliver and protect the site.</p>
      <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>VoxelCurve does not currently describe any advertising or third-party behavioral analytics integration in this policy. If advertising, analytics or consent tooling is enabled later, this policy should be updated before or when those services are activated to identify the relevant providers and choices.</p>
      <h2>Public issue tracker</h2>
      <p>Technical reports submitted to the VoxelCurve GitHub issue tracker are public and are governed by GitHub's own terms and privacy practices. Do not post sensitive personal information, credentials or private files in an issue.</p>
      <h2>Your controls</h2>
      <p>You can remove locally stored VoxelCurve progress through your browser's site-data controls. You can also use VoxelCurve without sharing blueprint links or generated files.</p>
    </div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
